   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**In 2025, 732 million adults could not read and write a simple statement**, down from 806 million in 2000.\n\n- **63%** of them are women (461 million).\n- **Central and Southern Asia** has the most: 344 million, 47% of the world's total.\n\nThe dashboard shows the trend since 2000 by sex, and the SDG regions with an estimate for 2025; a map beside it shows the countries where they live. These are UIS estimates for adults aged 15 and over. Source: UIS, November 2026 release; indicators ILLPOP.AG15T99, ILLPOP.AG15T99.F, ILLPOP.AG15T99.M.",
